# spec_id: eravos.organism.retro-dco · version 1.0.0 · phase P139 · status built 2026-11-06 (his go: "Build it.", after the UI preview)
# the design (lineage, components, depth audit, packs): tools/music/planned/retro-dco.spec · the face: tools/music/planned/retro-dco.ui.md
identity:
  id: eravos.retro-dco ; label: Retro DCO ; icon: 🌃 ; accent: #3be8ff ; category: genre instruments
  comp_intent: Retro Poly's sound family and face, rebuilt from the shared components, with the 80s DCO polys' depth
ports:
  out: audio (stereo) · in: notes (note_in), MIDI (armed), key (theory_in), transport (tick: the arp) · mod_in: cutoff (cents), pwm, res, drift
params: Retro Poly's 26 face controls (same names and defaults; res is 0…1 here) + Voice, Filter, Drive + 26 under More depth
  (voice cards, poly-mod + hard sync, LFO with delay, velocity, BBD chorus, unison, sub and noise) — every one an AudioParam (live)
signal_dag (per voice card, in one AudioWorklet from the components' own kernel text):
  random-source (drift) ─┐            lfo (+ delay fade) ─┐       env-adsr (filter) ─┐
  voice-allocator → note → pitch (glide, card offset) ──→ osc-va saw + pulse (× unison-stack, hard sync) + osc-sub + osc-noise
    → filter-svf 24 dB | filter-ladder (drive) ← cutoff (keytrack, env, velocity, LFO, card, mod) → × env-adsr (amp, velocity)
  all cards → filter-svf HPF → bbd-line → ensemble-core (Juno I / II / I+II, as data) → mix → level → out
decisions:
  - A, not B (2026-11-06): a new tool beside Retro Poly; Retro Poly stays as it is. Making it Retro Poly's engine (B) waits for his ear —
    Retro Poly's presets draw random drift, so a null render cannot prove "no change" yet
  - the voice allocator runs on the main thread (it decides); the worklet only plays cards (16 slots: trigger, gate, note, velocity)
  - the chorus: bbd-line at the mode's base delay (stages 256 = the Juno's chip) into ensemble-core taps at 0.5 ms
gaps (open, none hidden):
  - the arp is Retro Poly's code copied (it moves to the shared arp component — the planned spec's depth_audit)
  - chord-memory mode (chord-engine) not yet · packs: Factory 12 presets; the eight planned packs (≥ 6 each) not yet
  - hard sync is not band-limited at the reset (aliases at high ratios) · cpu per voice not yet measured in build/perf.mjs

